course: dictionary
lesson: 1581
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning is right. The word chaser is a good example. «A border collie called Chaser learned the names of over 1,000 toys.» Here Chaser is a dog's name, because it starts with a capital letter and it is the dog's name, not the word for something that chases.
explain: The word chaser on its own means a person or animal that chases someone or something. In a game of tag, the chaser is the one who tries to catch the others. In science, a storm chaser follows storms to study or film them. In both cases, the word tells you someone is going after something.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around the word and then test it. Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If you are not sure, the clues around the word will usually settle it.
fact: A chaser is a person or animal who chases someone or something.
fact: In sport, a steeplechaser is a horse that races over fences.
fact: A storm chaser is a person who follows storms to study or film them.
fact: In the Harry Potter books, Quidditch has players called chasers.
fact: «Chaser» can also be a dog's name, as in «A border collie called Chaser learned the names of over 1,000 toys.»
exercise: «A border collie called Chaser learned the names of over 1,000 toys.» Is Chaser here a dog's name or a word for something that chases? | *A dog's name | A storm | A toy | A game of tag
exercise: In science, what does a storm chaser do? | *Follows storms to study or film them | Hides from storms in a cave | Builds houses that stand up to wind | Sells umbrellas on rainy days
exercise: What is a steeplechaser? | *A horse that races over fences | A fast train that runs on steep hills | A runner who wears spiked shoes | A bird that dives into water
test: In the game of tag, who is the chaser? | The one who is always caught | *The one who tries to catch the others | The one who keeps score
test: In the Harry Potter game Quidditch, what is a chaser? | *A player in the game | A bird that lives in the castle | A spell used to fly | A broom for sweeping the pitch
exam: Which meaning fits «The chaser drove after the storm to film the tornado»? | A child who runs away from storms | A dog that learns the names of toys | *A person who follows storms to study or film them | A cloud that hides the sun
